{"key":"ics/T1692.002","id":"T1692.002","name":"Reporting Message","domain":"ics","platforms":[],"environments":["ics-ot"],"source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1692/002","technique_page":"techniques/ics/T1692.002/","page":"detections/ics/T1692.002/","status":"guidance_only","counts":{"sigma":0,"atlas_basic":0,"atlas_anomaly":0,"strategies":1,"analytics":1,"live_validated":0},"sigma_rules":[],"atlas_basic":[],"atlas_anomaly":[],"anomaly_types":[],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0746","name":"Detection of Spoof Reporting Message","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0746","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--c0e6c96d-8605-407a-9bce-628e7853b07f","relationship_id":"relationship--81fd1ae0-e3ef-40b7-86d8-89c85fd86100","description":"","analytics":[{"id":"AN1879","name":"Analytic 1879","guidance":"Various techniques enable spoofing a reporting message. Consider monitoring for Rogue Master and Adversary-in-the-Middle activity which may precede this technique.\nMonitor asset logs for alarms or other information the adversary is unable to directly suppress. Relevant alarms include those from a loss of communications due to Adversary-in-the-Middle activity.\nVarious techniques enable spoofing a reporting message. Monitor for LLMNR/NBT-NS poisoning via new services/daemons which may be used to enable this technique. For added context on adversary procedures and background see Name Resolution Poisoning and SMB Relay.\nSpoofed reporting messages may be detected by reviewing the content of automation protocols, either through detecting based on expected values or comparing to other out of band process data sources. Spoofed messages may not precisely match legitimate messages which may lead to malformed traffic, although traffic may be malformed for many benign reasons. Monitor reporting messages for changes in how they are constructed.\n\nVarious techniques enable spoofing a reporting message. Consider monitoring for Rogue Master and Adversary-in-the-Middle activity.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0746#AN1879","platforms":["None"],"tuning":[],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"Network Traffic","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1879","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0746#AN1879","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"component_id":"DC0108","component":"Device Alarm","name":"Operational Databases","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1879","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0746#AN1879","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0108/"},{"component_id":"DC0063","component":"Windows Registry Key Modification","name":"Windows Registry","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1879","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0746#AN1879","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0063/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"Network Traffic","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1879","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0746#AN1879","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0108","name":"Device Alarm","tag":"Device Alarm","page":"telemetry/DC0108/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","tag":"Network Traffic Content","page":"telemetry/DC0085/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","tag":"Network Traffic Flow","page":"telemetry/DC0078/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","tag":"Windows Registry Key Modification","page":"telemetry/DC0063/","kind":"attack_component"}],"visibility":"source_mapped","vi